# So when showing b.ts: "├▷│" (a.ts has child, so │ from a.ts)
# When showing c.ts: "└▷││" (both a.ts and b.ts have children, so ││ from a.ts and b.ts)
# 
# Then d.ts is shown below c.ts with both pipes connecting: "  └┴─▷d.ts"
# Where: "  " (c.ts was last, no more siblings from root), "└" (last of a.ts's children), 
# "┴" (b.ts's connection merges), "─" (extension), "▷" (arrow)

